Here are both approaches for Shell navigation in .NET MAUI:

**1. Register the route**
```csharp
// AppShell.xaml.cs
Routing.RegisterRoute("productdetails", typeof(ProductDetailsPage));
```

**2. Navigate from ProductListPage**
```csharp
// Approach A – simple string parameter
async void OnProductSelected(Product product)
{
    await Shell.Current.GoToAsync($"productdetails?productId={product.Id}");
}

// Approach B – pass the full object
async void OnProductSelected(Product product)
{
    var navParams = new Dictionary<string, object>
    {
        { "product", product }
    };
    await Shell.Current.GoToAsync("productdetails", navParams);
}
```

**3. Receive data in the ViewModel with `IQueryAttributable`**
```csharp
public class ProductDetailsViewModel : ObservableObject, IQueryAttributable
{
    private string _productId;
    private Product _product;

    public string ProductId { get => _productId; set => SetProperty(ref _productId, value); }
    public Product Product  { get => _product;  set => SetProperty(ref _product, value); }

    public void ApplyQueryAttributes(IDictionary<string, object> query)
    {
        // Approach A – string parameter arrives as a string
        if (query.TryGetValue("productId", out var id))
            ProductId = id.ToString();

        // Approach B – full object arrives as-is (no serialization)
        if (query.TryGetValue("product", out var obj) && obj is Product p)
            Product = p;
    }
}
```

**4. Wire the ViewModel to the page**
```csharp
public partial class ProductDetailsPage : ContentPage
{
    public ProductDetailsPage(ProductDetailsViewModel vm)
    {
        InitializeComponent();
        BindingContext = vm;
    }
}
```

**Key differences:**

| | String param (`?key=val`) | Object param (dictionary) |
|---|---|---|
| **Data types** | Strings only | Any object |
| **Serialization** | URL-encoded | Passed by reference |
| **Multiple values** | Chain with `&` | Add more dict entries |
| **Back-navigation** | Survives back nav | May be null on back nav |

> **Tip:** For the object approach, the `Product` instance is passed by reference — it's not serialized. If you need data to survive process restarts, persist the ID and reload from a service inside `ApplyQueryAttributes`.
